        <p>No ! if you do, and you have a cald you aro risking a quick and painful death trona pneumonia or consumption. Once yon taloa cud your overy ar and endeavoer should be to get rid et it, especially if is accompanied by cosoghing, ay every cough is anothnr nail in your coffin. Read the following from a well• knowu gentleman : Llantair Vicarage, Ruthin, July 12, 1893</p>
        <p>Drar Sirs.—As to the efficacy of Lavans Lung Liactus, I tog to state that I have found it most useful in the (-Arty stages of a cold. Taken at the very beginning, it stops the further progress cf tha malady, and it is cer- tainly useful in any stage or a cold, and moreover it is a very safe, and a most ayroeshle medicine to take. I hope that this rocommecthtion may be useful to you in promoting the sale of the Linctus. I am, yours faithfully, (Rev.) BASIL M. JONES.</p>
