        <p>Action Against a Warrington Company. In the Chancery of Lanca,hire at Liverpool on Monday the ease of Baxendale v. the Hope Foundry Company, Limited, was heard. This was a naotion by the plaiW-iff, George Baxendale, on behalf of he debenture holder in the defendant company, who</p>
        <p>. _ carry on business at Da Dam-lane, Warrington, for a declaration that the mortgage debentures issued by the defendant, company, and now out,tuliding should constitute a charge upon all the property of the company comprised therein. Mr Loraine (in- structed by Messrs Evans, Lockett, and Co., Liver- pool) appeared for the plaintiff, the company not baling represented. The Court granted the usual order.</p>
