        <p>At a meeting of the above clinmiqqe it was resolved " that P.C. Barnett bo ppniuted a s-ry,eant." Q. On the motion of the MAYOR, seconded by Alderman 'TJTTON, the minutt.4 wee -doted. Finance and Estate Committee.</p>
        <p>•-- A meeting of thi c un:nittee was held on April 9th, when it was resolved " Th it the Borough Surveyor Zborized to have the stebles b2l,riging to the Queen's tf'l eat into a sanitary cowl-lon, at an estimated cost occ42,'' and" that th- fl or of the ahop bs Sankey.-,trot at :„4 by Mr. F. J. D 4 his lowercd ts the stoat level AfeStilhated VW of £22" secoluelr.", 411 FAIRCLOUGH itiOved. and Couneillor MoNxs reeed. the approval 43'• the minutfll, which were con- Improvement and Lighting Committee Purchase of Bridge street Property. Important Recommendations. At a meeting of ;is committee it was resolved " That Plane ot several buildings, &amp;a.. in tile borough 100 ap- Droved. At a entigequent moeting held on April 3rd, it Was resolved "That the read from Warrington Bridge to the Swing Bridge over the canal at Lat-Mford be narn•Al Xnutsford-road." and at a rurther meetinz held on April 19% it was resnlved "That no plans of buildings from Which the rain water is prlpcged to be discharged upon the footpaths be anoroved." It was resolved " That the eau of £4,200 be paid to Mr William Fletcher for the Purchase of his premises at Bridge-foot." nw izowitu resolutions passed by the Gene.ral Purposes Committee Were adopted by this committee :—" That the sum of Q 550 be paid tie Mr Ralph Johnson for the purchase of a striper land and the alterations of his premises at the corner of Rvlands-street and Bridge-street." " That the BUlti of £515 and costs be paid to Mr Benjamin Grim- ier the purchase of his premises in Upper Bank- Striet.'"rhat the sum of £525 be paid to Mr Wilfiam TWISS for the purchase of his premises at the corner of Asadainy-street and Mtrsev-street." Alderataa BUTTON, in moving the adoption of the hainutes, referred to the purchases of land. Ths.y were aware the purch4s.s were for the purpose of street ins- Oravemeats. The resolution referring to the sum of f 550 to be paid to Mr Ralph Johnson for the strip of rd and alterations of the premiss at