        <p>Volunteer Parade. 10, At Lynam on Saturday the menabere of 11 (Lyto Company of the 3rd V.B. Cheshire Regite paraded at Deansgreen, the residence of CaptBl7,o G Groves, and after a few movements unde,!.jr command of the Captain and 6ieutenant T4lO way, the men were inspected by Colonel IT id Mothersill, V.D. The Colonel took the opportoo.of of presenting ex-'SergPant Peter Platt, of gelloo croft, who for over 20 years was a member° yet Lymm company, with the leng service ineuatol good conduct. The Colonel expressed a bepe,M many of those present would continue in the 74 as volunteers until they had the honour of eargoo, the medal. Mrs. Groves, wife of Captain Grlcil then pinned the medal on Mr. Platt's coat. of 15 years since ex-Sergeant Platt left the Volu°idet force, but he will be well remembered by th!.:00 generation of Volunteers in Lyinm. The Plhof company is now almost up to full strength, ,'":104 being close on 40 recruits this year, several Or from the Latchford and Warrington neighboll%dsi, The company will go into camp on Whit Stl'or at Salisbury Plain, the bulk for a fortnight. tor some for the whole month asked for by the 001 ment.</p>
